paraphrases:[P('old people','older adults','senior citizens','people in later life','older adults中性自然，适合多数语境。'),P('people live longer','longevity is increasing','life expectancy is rising','more people survive into old age','life expectancy适合数据讨论。'),P('care for the elderly','support older people','provide later-life care','meet older adults’ care needs','meet needs强调服务是否匹配。'),P('fewer babies are born','the birth rate is falling','fertility is declining','births are becoming less numerous','fertility常用于人口研究。'),P('retire later','extend working lives','remain in employment for longer','delay departure from the workforce','extend working lives适合政策讨论。'),P('lonely older people','socially isolated seniors','older adults with limited social contact','people cut off from community life','isolated不等于独居。'),P('cost of pensions','pension expenditure','the fiscal burden of retirement income','public spending on pension provision','fiscal burden带有成本压力含义。'),P('use older workers’ skills','retain experienced employees','draw on senior staff’s expertise','make productive use of accumulated experience','retain强调避免人才过早流失。')],
sentences:[S('As + population trend + continues, + service or institution + will need to + response.','随着某种人口趋势持续，相关服务或机构将需要采取相应措施。','As life expectancy continues to rise, health services will need to provide more long-term care.'),S('Older adults who + situation + are more likely to + outcome than those who + contrasting situation.','处于某种情况的老年人，比处于相反情况的人更可能出现某种结果。','Older adults who maintain regular social contact are more likely to stay healthy than those who become isolated.'),S('By enabling + group + to + action, + policy + can both + benefit one + and + benefit two.','通过帮助某群体采取行动，某项政策可以同时带来两方面益处。','By enabling experienced staff to work flexible hours, employers can both retain expertise and reduce labour shortages.')],
